# xways-bulk_extractor — Claude Code notes

> **Per-X-Tension instructions for Claude Code.** Copy this file to `CLAUDE.md`
> (git-ignored) in this folder and tailor it for your environment. Claude reads
> `CLAUDE.md` as directory-level instructions. Keep this committed `.example`
> **generic — no local paths, credentials, or case data.**
>
> Project-wide rules live in the repo-root `CLAUDE.md` and the authoring skill
> (`xways-xtension-authoring`). This file captures only what is specific to
> **xways-bulk_extractor**.

## What this X-Tension is

Wrapper around Simson Garfinkel's `bulk_extractor` for X-Ways Forensics.
Three input modes (active evidence-object image, picked file/dir, right-click
selected items) and three output integrations (add output dir to the case via
`XWF_CreateEvObj`, open in Explorer, feature-file hit tagging via `XWF_Label`).

- **Stem / DLL:** `xways-bulk_extractor` → `xways-bulk_extractor.dll`
- **Version:** `0.5.0-beta` — keep `VERSION` in the `.cpp`, the `.rc`
  VERSIONINFO, and the README in lockstep (versioning convention).
- **Identity constants** (top of `xways-bulk_extractor.cpp`): `NAME`,
  `VERSION`, `DESCRIPTION`, `REPORT_TABLE_SCANNED`, `REPORT_TABLE_PREFIX`.

## Build

```powershell
<path-to-skill>/scripts/build-xtension.ps1 -Name xways-bulk_extractor
```

Close X-Ways first — the DLL is locked while it runs (no hot reload).

## Threading model (do not regress)

The settings dialog hosts the run on a **joinable** worker thread
(`g_workerThread`), but the worker runs **only the subprocess phase**
(`ExecuteBeRun`). Every `XWF_*` call stays on X-Ways' own thread:

- **A `PrepareRunInput`** — item extraction + tag-scanned labels; runs in the
  IDOK handler before the worker starts.
- **B `ExecuteBeRun`** — validate/identity-gate the binary, spawn/wait BE;
  the only phase on the worker. Watches `g_cancelRequested` every 100 ms and
  `TerminateProcess`es the child on cancel.
- **C `PostProcessRun`** — `XWF_CreateEvObj`, feature-hit `XWF_Label`
  tagging, temp cleanup; runs in the `WM_APP_DONE` handler.

The worker is reaped in `WM_APP_DONE` and (safety net) in `XT_Done` — never
detach it, and never move an `XWF_*` call into phase B.

## Wrapped tool / dependencies

- **bulk_extractor v2.x** for Windows — analyst supplies the binary
  (`bulk_extractor64.exe` next to the DLL is auto-detected; cfg `be_binary`
  overrides). Identity gate: PE VERSIONINFO / `-h` banner needle
  `bulk_extractor` (`VerifyHelperIdentity`), enforced at Browse, the IDOK
  pre-run gate, and inside `ExecuteBeRun`.
- **WSL mode** (optional): runs a Linux `bulk_extractor` via `wsl.exe`
  (cfg `wsl_be_binary` / auto-detection). The Linux binary cannot be
  PE-inspected from Windows — the identity gate only applies to native mode.

## Config & sidecar files

`bulk_extractor.cfg` next to the DLL (live cfg is git-ignored; only
`xways-bulk_extractor.cfg.example` is committed). Keys: `be_binary`,
`wsl_be_binary`, `use_wsl_default`, `keep_temp_dir`, `default_output_dir`
(intentionally **not** written on save — output follows the case:
`<caseRoot>\xways-bulk_extractor\…`).

## Gotchas / notes

- A reused (non-empty) output dir is analyst error: pre-2.2.0 BE refuses to
  run; BE 2.2.0's restart logic instead exits 0 having silently processed
  nothing. The X-Tension suggests a fresh per-run subdir and just logs what
  BE reports otherwise.
- BE hard-errors on `-e`/`-x` with a scanner name it doesn't know (`no such
  scanner`, exit 5) — so unchecking a 2.2.0-only scanner (`vin`, `rtti`)
  against a pre-2.2.0 binary fails the run. Deliberate: no version-gating.
- Selected-items mode needs a volume handle: invoked from the Case Root
  window, `hVolume` is NULL (21.4 SR-5 behavior) and the run is refused with
  an explanation.
- Selected-items extraction happens on the UI thread before the worker
  starts, so a huge right-click selection blocks the dialog during export —
  the long BE run itself is async and cancellable.
- `XT_Finalize` returns `0x02` ("save volume snapshot") when the run added
  labels or an evidence object.

## Conventions in play

Output directory, verbose logging, helper-exe verification, Ctrl-to-save
(Ctrl+Run = save cfg, Ctrl+Close = Save as…), subprocess stdio, add-output-
to-case — see the authoring skill's `docs/conventions/`.

## Don't commit

Compiled `xways-bulk_extractor.dll`, `bulk_extractor64.exe`, live `.cfg`,
local paths (`C:\Users\…`), or case data. See the repo-hygiene convention.
